      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Samantha_The_Demoncat\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"29654\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/samantha_the_demoncat/48/5378_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Samantha_The_Demoncat:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fanatic says trans rights?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>“You were commanded to LOVE YOUR NEIGHBOR, not deny who they truly are! How dare you place your preconceptions about flesh cloud your eyes to the soul!” <em>SMITE!</em> (Insert JoCat’s smite sound effect from Crap Guide to Paladin)</p>\n<p>Or maybe it’s just the 30+ year D&amp;D player in me that gets annoyed when Paladin-types are portrayed as following the “lawful” part more than the “good” part of their alignment…</p>",
