      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/escher/{size}/4865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-09-28T04:16:41.198Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Card Shark confuses me, because isn’t Kaargra already basically a shark person? Are they the same species or is this a SECOND “shark people” species?</p>\n<p>I did love the mental image of space zombies stealing the Pink Lady. That sounds like something that ought to be drawn by Rat Fink.</p>\n<p>The thing about the energy-boot reminded me of an old D&amp;D joke. The PCs are just really determined to get through a door the DM doesn’t want them to get through. The door is locked, barred from inside, and made of adamantine so they can’t break it.  The hinges are also adamantine.  The players look at it for a while, then one says, “What’s the wall made of?”</p>\n<p>Greazer (thinking): “Uncool. A Thneedarian energy-shackle. Virtually unbreakable.”<br>\n&lt;opens trunk, gets out cutter&gt;<br>\n“But they always forget…”<br>\n<br>\n“…to wonder what the floor is made of.”<br>\n</p>",
